---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Counters"
  description="Compare grow-only, positive-negative, and sequenced distributed counters."
  territory="Structures"
  sheetTitle="Counters"
>
  <article class="counter-family">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="territory-label">Structure family</p>
      <h1>Counters</h1>
      <p>
        A shared number looks simple until several replicas change it at once.
        Counter designs differ in which changes they permit and what they must
        remember so repeated or reordered messages stay safe.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="g-counter-title">
      <header>
        <div>
          <p class="structure-kind">CRDT</p>
          <h2 id="g-counter-title">G-counter</h2>
          <p>A grow-only counter for independent increments.</p>
        </div>
        <code>g_counter_kernel</code>
      </header>
      <div class="structure-body">
        <div>
          <p>
            Each replica owns one component and can only raise it. Merge keeps
            the largest value for every replica, so duplicate and reordered
            messages do not change the result.
          </p>
          <h3>Best for</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Distributed metrics and tallies that never decrease</li>
            <li>At-least-once delivery where an increment may arrive again</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Updates</dt><dd>Increment only</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Merge rule</dt><dd>Per-replica maximum</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Metadata</dt><dd>One integer per replica</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <a class="structure-link" href="/structures/g-counter/">Read the G-counter lesson</a>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="pn-counter-title">
      <header>
        <div>
          <p class="structure-kind">CRDT</p>
          <h2 id="pn-counter-title">PN-counter</h2>
          <p>A counter that preserves concurrent additions and corrections.</p>
        </div>
        <code>pn_counter_kernel</code>
      </header>
      <div class="structure-body">
        <div>
          <p>
            A PN-counter pairs two G-counters. One records positive changes and
            the other records negative changes. Each half merges by
            per-replica maximum, then the counter subtracts the negative total.
          </p>
          <h3>Best for</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Offline counters that must increase and decrease</li>
            <li>Corrections that may be delivered more than once</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Updates</dt><dd>Increment and decrement</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Merge rule</dt><dd>Maximum on both component sets</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Metadata</dt><dd>Two integers per replica</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <a class="structure-link" href="/structures/pn-counter/">Read the PN-counter lesson</a>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="shared-counter-title">
      <header>
        <div>
          <p class="structure-kind">DDS</p>
          <h2 id="shared-counter-title">SharedCounter</h2>
          <p>A signed counter whose operations pass through one sequencer.</p>
        </div>
        <code>counter_kernel</code>
      </header>
      <div class="structure-body">
        <div>
          <p>
            Each replica sends signed deltas to a sequencer. The sequencer
            assigns one sequence number and broadcasts the numbered operation.
            Replicas apply each sequence number once.
          </p>
          <h3>Best for</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Shared totals under an ordered collaborative runtime</li>
            <li>Small summaries where a sequencer already coordinates updates</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Updates</dt><dd>Signed integer deltas</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Application rule</dt><dd>Apply each sequence number once</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Metadata</dt><dd>One integer plus pending operations</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <a class="structure-link" href="/structures/shared-counter/">Read the SharedCounter lesson</a>
    </section>

    <nav class="structure-next" aria-label="Continue through structures">
      <a href="/structures/">Browse all structure families</a>
      <a href="/atlas/multi-value-registers/">Continue to registers</a>
    </nav>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .counter-family {
    max-width: var(--measure-reading);
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .page-intro {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-7);
  }

  .page-intro > p:last-child {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  .counter-family > section {
    position: relative;
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
    padding: var(--space-5);
    border: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
    background: var(--clear);
  }

  section > header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-5);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-4);
    border-bottom: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
  }

  section h2,
  section header p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  section h2 {
    margin-block: var(--space-1);
  }

  .structure-kind {
    color: var(--instrument);
    font-family: var(--font-data);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  section header code {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .structure-body {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.3fr) minmax(15rem, 0.7fr);
    gap: var(--space-6);
    padding-block: var(--space-5);
  }

  .structure-body p,
  .structure-body h3 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .structure-body h3 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .structure-body ul {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  dl {
    margin: 0;
    border-block: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
  }

  dl div {
    padding-block: var(--space-3);
  }

  dl div + div {
    border-top: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line-faint);
  }

  dt {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  dd {
    margin: var(--space-1) 0 0;
  }

  .structure-link {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .structure-next {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
    padding-block: var(--space-5);
    border-top: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  @media (width < 42rem) {
    .counter-family > section {
      padding: var(--space-4);
    }

    section > header,
    .structure-body {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    section > header {
      display: grid;
      gap: var(--space-2);
    }
  }
</style>
